## Known v0.1 issues (must fix before v0.2)

1. ✅ `transforms/numbers.ts::obfuscateNumbers` does NOT actually mutate the
   token stream usefully — the pipeline redoes D2 on the AST instead.
   Decision: kept as-is (documented). The pipeline-level D2 wins.
2. ✅ `src/transforms/identifier.ts::buildMapping` only emits single-char
   names; for >53 names it produces a 2-char scheme that uses positions
   `0..25` and `0..51` and may collide. Replaced with an injectively-mapped
   scheme (a/b/c/.../z/aa/.../az/ba/...).
3. ✅ `parse()` does NOT round-trip — e.g. hex literals are kept as raw
   strings; `(function ...) end` with a table-string call arg may emit
   wrong. **Two fixed bugs in v0.1**: `parseConcat` was passing `minPrec=5`
   to `parseBinop` which silently dropped `==` / `<` etc.; and the
   `parseFnDeclTail` call for `local function NAME` was passing `parts: []`
   instead of `[nameTok.value]`, producing an anonymous function AST.
4. ✅ The emit `'__STR__'` synthetic token in
   `transforms/strings.ts::obfuscateStrings` is dead code — the pipeline
   walks the AST and never sees the token. Safe to delete.

Additional bugs found during end-to-end testing (Luau 0.601):

5. ✅ **String cipher key representation**: emitter was passing the key as a
   hex *string* but the runtime decoder was indexing it like an array,
   producing garbled output. Fix: emit the key as a Lua array literal
   `{0xAC, 0x72, 0x31, 0x60}`.
6. ✅ **String cipher index arithmetic**: the runtime decoder used
   `i` and `(i-1)` for byte-index/key-index, off-by-one from the
   encryption formula. Fix: align to `(j+1)%4+1, j)` where `j = (i+1)/2 - 1`
   is the 0-based byte index of the current byte being decoded.
7. ✅ **Anonymous function expressions are not emitted with body**. FIXED in
   v0.1.1: `exprToLuau` case `"Function"` now recursively emits body
   statements with proper indentation, wrapped in `function(params)\n ... \nend`.
8. ✅ **Function parameters are not renamed**. FIXED in v0.1.1: the
   `collectCandidateIdents()` function now adds function parameter names to
   the declared set (when each param is declared exactly once in the file).

